          m1=1: I \ B_1 = I itself (l = 5/28), so B_m2 alone must cover I: needs 5/28 <= 1/(4 m2), i.e. m2 <= 7/5, i.e. m2 = 1 <= m1. Impossible.
          m1=2: I \ B_2 = I itself (l = 5/28), so B_m2 alone must cover I: needs 5/28 <= 1/(4 m2), i.e. m2 <= 7/5, i.e. m2 = 1 <= m1. Impossible.

